WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.319 --> 00:00:07.180
The war in Ukraine continues despite the Minsk
ceasefire agreement because it is rooted deeply

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:12.490
in ideological, geostrategic, and domestic
political goals of Vladimir Putin, Russia’s

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:17.830
likely president–for life.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.740
Russia has violated two ceasefire agreements.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:26.349
It continues to send troops, arms and heavy
equipment into Ukraine in support of its proxies,

00:00:26.349 --> 00:00:28.330
the so-called “separatists.”

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:33.620
And Russia will continue this war until it
achieves all of its goals there–or until

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:38.110
Vladimir Putin finds the domestic political
costs too high and will be forced to scale

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.149
down and to compromise.

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:43.430
So what is Putin seeking to achieve in Ukraine
and why?

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:49.920
Ideologically, Putin fancies himself the “gatherer”
of historically Russian lands.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:55.960
In his worldview, Russia is not only a country—it
is the center of a unique Eurasian civilization,

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.680
distinct from both Europe and Asia.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:03.079
Policies like the “Russian World” and
the “Eurasian Union” seek to fulfill this

00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:09.140
ideal: not a new Soviet Union but a Russia
militarily, politically and economically dominant

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:14.290
over much of Eurasia with a veto power over
the neighboring countries’ foreign policies

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:16.890
and domestic political arrangements as well.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:22.750
So a Europe­-bound Ukraine is a key, perhaps
fatal, obstacle to such a plan.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:27.880
Geostrategically Putin sees this new Russia
as a counterbalance to the United States and

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:34.100
the West, which, in his view, not only are
bent on world domination but first and foremost

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:39.170
are constantly scheming against Russia with
a goal of taking away its sovereignty.

00:01:39.170 --> 00:01:44.030
Domestic political considerations, however,
are by far the most important factor in Putin’s

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:45.500
policy in Ukraine.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:50.070
Before Russia’s “Ukrainian adventure”,
Putin’s popularity was at record lows.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:55.240
Promises of reforming and modernizing the
economy went unfulfilled, and Russians were

00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:00.430
left with the same corrupt, oil­-dependent
system that they have had for years.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:06.130
By contrast, the patriotic mobilization and
the anti­-West hysteria, unleashed by the

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:10.750
state controlled television, have made the
President into the defender of the Motherland,

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:17.610
accounting for his astronomic ratings – which
is the only reliable part of the regime’s

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:18.610
legitimacy.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:21.190
But it is a two-edged political sword.

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:26.020
If Russia is seen to have achieved anything
short of a total victory in Ukraine, there

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:30.360
is likely to be a sharp downfall in Putin’s
personal popularity.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:34.820
This should be especially troubling for the
regime, given that Russia’s economy is sliding

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:40.350
into full-blown economic crisis, with the
ruble plummeting and inflation heating up.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:45.590
So Putin needs a victory that would include
not just a permanent dismemberment of Ukraine

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:51.080
but also its destabilization and ultimately
the replacement of the current pro­-European

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.600
regime in Kiev with a Russian puppet.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.850
So, what can the West do about this?

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:01.670
Given Russia’s military advantage over Ukraine,
a quick victory on the battlefield is out

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:02.670
of the question.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:08.510
Instead, a patient, long-term strategy is
needed—one which would include, but not

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:13.760
be limited to, arming and training Ukrainian
forces in order to raise the domestic costs

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:18.730
of Putin’s aggression: both in treasure
and, most importantly, in blood.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:22.250
Putin will in Ukraine for as long as he needs
to.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:27.230
So if the West is serious in thwarting his
plans, it needs to have just as much patience

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.030
and resolve.

